Settings of record: 9 samples, stride 174, m = 1046..2440, each at the
precision its own shard entry records.  Wall clock 260s single-core.

This is a SAMPLE, not a reproduction.  The full extension is ~9.4 core-hours
(delta_arb scales near m^2.6: 4.7s at m=1046, 69.6s at m=2440) and the
original run used 256 cores.  What the sample establishes is that the
committed shards were produced by the delta_arb in this tree at the
precisions they record -- it would catch a drifted precision rule, a
truncated shard, or a stride off-by-one.  It would not catch a wrong value
at an m that was not sampled.
